            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for to bless, then the Kannada for a wedding party."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಕಾಣೆಯಾಗು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಾಣೆಯಾಗು — kāṇeyāgu — \"to go missing\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಒಂದು ವೇಳೆ ಮಗು ಕಾಣೆಯಾದರೆ ಅಪ್ಪ ಅಮ್ಮ ತಕ್ಷಣ ದೂರು ಕೊಡುತ್ತಾರೆ. ondu vēḷe magu kāṇeyādare appa amma takṣaṇa dūru koḍuttāre. If a child goes missing, the parents report it at once."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): ಕಾಣೆಯಾಯಿತು, kāṇeyāyitu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಾಣೆ, not to be seen, and ಆಗು, to become."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಾಣೆಯಾಗು (kāṇeyāgu) is a native Dravidian compound: ಕಾಣೆ, \"not seen\", from kāṇ \"to see\" (DEDR 1443), and āgu \"to become\" (DEDR 333)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
